<title>NETHERLANDS: Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stocks mixed.</title>
<headline>Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stocks mixed.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil product inventories held in independent tankage in the Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp area were estimated to be at the following levels currently, a week ago and a year ago, industry sources said.</p>
<p>All figures in thousands of tonnes:</p>
<p>			16/1/97		   9/1/97	     19/1/96</p>
<p>    Gasoline	475-500			475		   500</p>
<p>    Naphtha		75		    50-75		    50</p>
<p>    Gas oil	   1,850		    1,950		 1,650</p>
<p>    Fuel oil	325-350			300		   300</p>
<p>    Jet kero	  20-25			 25		    15</p>
<p>Gasoline stocks rose slightly in a slow market with some incoming cargoes, although a couple of companies swiftly moved product by barge to Germany.</p>
<p>Naphtha inventories were also up on cargo arrivals.</p>
<p>Gas oil stocks fell noticeably as nominations were diverted from refineries, some of whom had little product available, to storage facilities. IPE delivery has just started.</p>
<p>Fuel oil rose as majors oversupplied the market and the bunker sector failed to absorb additional volumes.</p>
<p>Jef fuel stocks were down as some product left to be blended with the gas oil pool.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom, +31 20 504 5004</p>
</text>
